The regrade reproduces every pass count in my notes. Now the pooled confirmation table, edited minus start, per category, with paired standard errors over the same items. I will show it separately for:

- the v2 passes (7, 8), whose edit had the arity pair as well;
- the v3 passes (11, 12), which use the final edit;
- MBPP-style and HE-style prompts.

This is the table for the final report. It also shows whether any failure category grows systematically under v3.

```python
# Hypothesis: pooled over set-B confirmation passes, the edit lowers name-extension failures and leaves other categories flat; per-category paired diffs with SEs.
def cat2(c):
    if c.startswith('wi_'): return c if c in ('wi_extension','wi_other','wi_nodef') else 'wi_misc'
    if c in ('pass','arity','rt_TypeError','rt_NameError','syntax_error','cut','no_code','wrong_answer','timeout'): return c
    if c.startswith('rt_'): return 'rt_other'
    return c
CATS = ['pass','wi_extension','wi_other','wi_nodef','wi_misc','arity','rt_TypeError','rt_NameError','rt_other','syntax_error','timeout','cut','no_code','wrong_answer']
pairs = {}
for g in GA: pairs.setdefault((g['p'],g['item']), {})[g['m']] = g
def table(passes, kind):
    P = [v for (p,it),v in pairs.items() if p in passes and v['start']['kind']==kind]
    n = len(P); out = {}
    for c in CATS:
        d = np.array([(cat2(v['edited']['cls'])==c) - (cat2(v['start']['cls'])==c) for v in P], float)
        s = sum(cat2(v['start']['cls'])==c for v in P); e = sum(cat2(v['edited']['cls'])==c for v in P)
        out[c] = (s, e, 100*d.mean(), 100*d.std(ddof=1)/np.sqrt(n))
    return n, out
for lab, passes in (('v2 P7+P8',(7,8)),('v3 P11+P12',(11,12)),('ALL set-B',(7,8,11,12))):
    for kind in ('mbpp','he'):
        n,o = table(passes, kind)
        print(f'--- {lab} {kind} n={n}/model')
        print('   ', '  '.join(f"{c}:{o[c][0]}->{o[c][1]}({o[c][2]:+.1f}+-{o[c][3]:.1f})" for c in CATS if o[c][0] or o[c][1]))
```

Many of these NameErrors name the entry point itself: `min_length` (mbpp/528, in three separate start passes), `max_product` (mbpp/922) and `min_cost` (mbpp/1). Others name an extended variant of it, such as `listify_list_string`. The harness checks the entry point before running, so such code must contain a def with the given name that is not a module-level function when the test runs. Possible reasons are a nested def, a def inside a class or a `__main__` guard, or a call to the given name from a differently named def.

mbpp/528 is striking: start fails with this NameError in P7, P11 and P12, while v3 or v2 passes twice and gets a wrong answer once. I will read the start and edited code for mbpp/528 (P12) and mbpp/922 (P11) to see the structure.

```python
# Hypothesis: entry-point NameErrors come from code that names the module-level def differently (extension) but calls/defines the given name in a nested or test scope; the end-of-name repair removes the variant.
def show(p, nm, qid, n=420):
    for it,r in gen_cache[(p,nm)].items():
        e = r['id']; 
        g = [x for x in GA if x['p']==p and x['m']==nm and x['item']==it]
        if g and g[0]['qid']==qid:
            print(f'--- P{p} {nm} {qid} {g[0]["cls"]}'); print((r['code'] or '')[:n].encode('ascii','replace').decode()); return
show(12,'start','mbpp/528'); show(12,'edited','mbpp/528', 300)
show(11,'start','mbpp/922', 360)
```

The harness flags all three plain renames of the reference as wrong interface, so its check is not a substring test. But the start answer for mbpp/528 defines `min_length_lists` (an extension of `min_length`) and is graded as a NameError on `min_length`. The model's code probably also mentions the given name somewhere, for example in an example call, so the harness accepts the interface, runs the tests, and the call fails. Either way, these are wrong-name failures that my classification counted as NameErrors.

I will reclassify every NameError whose undefined name is the entry point as a wrong name. Its kind is set from the module-level defs: extension if a def starts with the given name, otherwise other or no def. Then I will recompute the pooled wrong-name table, so that the report counts extensions correctly for both models.

```python
# Hypothesis: reclassifying entry-point NameErrors as wrong names raises the extension count for start more than for edited (start 16+~6 vs edited 6+~2).
msg_cache = {}
def ne_msg(p, nm, it, qid):
    k=(p,nm,it)
    if k not in msg_cache: msg_cache[k] = my_run(gen_cache[(p,nm)][it]['code'], qid).get('msg') or ''
    return msg_cache[k]
def top_defs(code):
    try: return [n.name for n in ast.parse(code).body if isinstance(n,(ast.FunctionDef,ast.AsyncFunctionDef))]
    except Exception: return None
for g in GA:
    g['cls2'] = g['cls']
    if g['cls']=='rt_NameError' and g['kind'] in ('mbpp','he'):
        ep = mb[g['qid']]['test_format']['entry_point']
        msg = ne_msg(g['p'], g['m'], g['item'], g['qid'])
        und = _re.findall(r"name '(\w+)' is not defined", msg)
        if und and und[0]==ep:
            ds = top_defs(gen_cache[(g['p'],g['m'])][g['item']]['code']) or []
            g['cls2'] = 'wi_extension' if any(d.startswith(ep) and d!=ep for d in ds) else ('wi_nodef' if not ds else 'wi_other')
        elif und and ep in und[0]:
            g['cls2'] = 'ne_variant'   # calls an extended variant of the given name
pairs2 = {}
for g in GA: pairs2.setdefault((g['p'],g['item']), {})[g['m']] = g
def table2(passes, kind, cats):
    P = [v for (p,it),v in pairs2.items() if p in passes and v['start']['kind']==kind]; n=len(P); o={}
    for lab, cs in cats.items():
        f = lambda g: cat2(g['cls2']) in cs or g['cls2'] in cs
        d = np.array([f(v['edited'])-f(v['start']) for v in P], float)
        o[lab] = (sum(f(v['start']) for v in P), sum(f(v['edited']) for v in P), 100*d.mean(), 100*d.std(ddof=1)/np.sqrt(n))
    return n,o
CAT3 = {'pass':['pass'], 'ext':['wi_extension'], 'other_name':['wi_other','wi_misc'], 'nodef':['wi_nodef'], 'ALL_names':['wi_extension','wi_other','wi_misc','wi_nodef'],
        'ne_variant':['ne_variant'], 'arity':['arity'], 'TypeError_other':['rt_TypeError'], 'NameError_other':['rt_NameError'], 'other_rt':['rt_other'], 'syntax':['syntax_error'], 'cut':['cut'], 'wrong_answer':['wrong_answer']}
for lab, passes in (('v3 only P11+P12',(11,12)),('ALL set-B P7,P8,P11,P12',(7,8,11,12))):
    for kind in ('mbpp','he'):
        n,o = table2(passes, kind, CAT3)
        print(f'--- {lab} {kind} n={n}'); print('   ', '  '.join(f"{c}:{o[c][0]}->{o[c][1]}({o[c][2]:+.1f}+-{o[c][3]:.1f})" for c in CAT3 if o[c][0] or o[c][1]))
